Drop WASIX networking from the C API build.

`wasmer-c-api`'s `wasi` feature enables `wasmer-wasix/sys`, which includes
`host-reqwest` and so pulls in reqwest, rustls, `aws-lc-sys` and
`rustls-platform-verifier`. These need a newer binutils (aarch64) and macOS SDK
(x86_64) than BinaryBuilder's defaults, and make the library about 6 MB larger.
The C API does not need WASIX networking, so enable the same wasix features as
`sys` except `host-reqwest`, `journal` (does not compile without the others) and
the `webc/mmap` / `virtual-mio/sys` ones, which cannot be spelled in a
dependency feature list. WASI itself is unaffected.

Upstream: not yet reported.

diff --git a/lib/c-api/Cargo.toml b/lib/c-api/Cargo.toml
index aea8132..d6a4af7 100644
--- a/lib/c-api/Cargo.toml
+++ b/lib/c-api/Cargo.toml
@@ -36,7 +36,12 @@ wasmer-types = { version = "=7.5.0", path = "../types" }
 wasmer-wasix = { path = "../wasix", version = "=0.705.0", features = [
   "host-fs",
   "host-vnet",
-  "sys",
+  "sys-minimal",
+  "time",
+  "logging",
